<p class="fxbus-muted">
  Visual-only canvas mirror. Use for wrong-side reality, dream logic, mirror realms, dimensional inversions, cursed reflections, or sudden perspective shifts.
</p>

<p class="fxbus-muted">
  Mouse coordinates are remapped to match the flipped canvas. This is playable for simple player interaction, but GM interaction may feel clunky while tokens are moving.
</p>

<hr class="fxbus-divider"/>

<div class="fxbus-grid-2">
  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Axis</label>
    <select name="canvasMirrorAxis">
      <option value="x" selected>Horizontal</option>
      <option value="y">Vertical</option>
      <option value="xy">Both axes</option>
    </select>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Transition</label>
    <select name="canvasMirrorTransition">
      <option value="instant" selected>Instant</option>
      <option value="fold">Fold</option>
      <option value="realityRipple">Reality ripple</option>
      <option value="glitchSnap">Glitch snap</option>
    </select>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="form-group">
  <label>Transition duration (ms)</label>
  <input
    type="number"
    name="canvasMirrorTransitionMs"
    value="0"
    step="50"
    min="0"
    max="5000"
  />
</div>

<p class="fxbus-muted">
  Fold flips the live canvas into its mirrored state. Reality ripple briefly squashes and distorts the live canvas. Glitch snap adds a sharp digital displacement before settling into the mirror. Interaction remains remapped after the transition completes.
</p>

<hr class="fxbus-divider"/>

<div class="fxbus-row">
  <button type="button" class="fxbus-do" data-action="canvasMirrorStart">Apply</button>
  <button type="button" class="fxbus-do fxbus-smallbtn" data-action="canvasMirrorStop">Stop</button>
  <button type="button" class="fxbus-do fxbus-smallbtn" data-action="fxbusCopyToMacro">Copy to Macro</button>
</div>